WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:03.200
Welcome to our overview of Voice of the Customer Dashboard.

00:00:03.580 --> 00:00:11.151
On this dashboard, you can review the Customer Experience or CX Health of your offers, read customer

00:00:11.151 --> 00:00:16.940
comments, identify product and listing issues, and take recommended actions to resolve problems.

00:00:17.540 --> 00:00:21.800
You can access the Voice of the Customer Dashboard from the Seller Central Main Menu.

00:00:22.020 --> 00:00:26.420
On the Voice of the Customer Summary page, you'll see two main sections.

00:00:27.160 --> 00:00:30.600
The first section is the CX Health Breakdown of your listings.

00:00:31.240 --> 00:00:36.560
This metric helps you understand the performance of your offers relative to similar offers.

00:00:37.240 --> 00:00:41.120
It considers your recent orders and customer feedback about your products.

00:00:42.000 --> 00:00:45.780
Listings are grouped into five buckets from very poor to excellent.

00:00:46.280 --> 00:00:52.849
Use the filters to look at details such as specific listings, fulfillment channels, or CX Health

00:00:52.849 --> 00:00:53.260
Breakdown.

00:00:54.060 --> 00:01:01.166
The Fit Insights tab, if available, allows you to view brand aggregated insights for certain ASINs

00:01:01.166 --> 00:01:03.387
to identify causes of returns,

00:01:03.387 --> 00:01:06.940
review customer feedback, and resolve size chart defects.

00:01:07.980 --> 00:01:13.780
Use the Download Data button to populate a CSV file with the information on the Summary page.

00:01:13.940 --> 00:01:20.772
The second section of the page shows your listings and listing details, including your Negative

00:01:20.772 --> 00:01:23.960
Customer Experience, or NCX, Rate, and Reason.

00:01:25.100 --> 00:01:30.513
Reviewing these details provides insight into how you can improve customer satisfaction for your

00:01:30.513 --> 00:01:30.900
listings.

00:01:31.900 --> 00:01:37.700
Click See Details to be taken to the listings detail page where you can dive deeper in a listing.

00:01:38.340 --> 00:01:41.160
The listings detail page has three sections.

00:01:41.840 --> 00:01:47.630
The first section shows a graph of your NCX Rate for that product with a benchmark trend to compare

00:01:47.630 --> 00:01:48.240
it to.

00:01:48.920 --> 00:01:55.304
Use the filter to select a time frame between 1 and 12 weeks to see how your rate has changed over

00:01:55.304 --> 00:01:56.520
a given time period.

00:01:57.300 --> 00:02:01.260
The next section shows the top reported customer issue for the product.

00:02:01.340 --> 00:02:08.369
Click See Details to get a more granular look at the top reported reason and understand the root

00:02:08.369 --> 00:02:08.760
cause.

00:02:09.080 --> 00:02:14.320
After reviewing the issue summary, click Resolve Issues to view recommended actions.

00:02:15.080 --> 00:02:20.500
These recommendations are specifically tailored to help address the top reported customer issues.

00:02:21.080 --> 00:02:24.540
Click Launch to go to the designated page to take action.

00:02:25.220 --> 00:02:28.680
The last section shows recent customer feedback for your listings.

00:02:29.360 --> 00:02:35.643
Here, you can read the customer feedback through various sources, including returns, to better understand

00:02:35.643 --> 00:02:36.900
the customer feedback.

00:02:37.860 --> 00:02:41.480
This concludes our overview of Voice of the Customer Dashboard.

00:02:42.140 --> 00:02:46.250
To learn more and stay up to date with Voice of the Customer enhancements,

00:02:46.250 --> 00:02:49.480
review the Voice of the Customer Help page in Seller Central.

00:02:50.040 --> 00:02:56.060
Be sure to check out our resource Managing Your Seller Feedback after watching this video.

00:02:56.960 --> 00:02:59.820
Thank you and happy selling in the Amazon Store!
